# CQROS Testing Standards

## Mission

Testing is mandatory.

No implementation is considered complete until it is tested.

Testing verifies

Correctness

Determinism

Reproducibility

Performance

Reliability

Safety

Architecture compliance

Testing is part of implementation.

Never treat it as optional.

---

# Testing Philosophy

CQROS follows

Test First Thinking

Every feature should have tests before production approval.

Every bug must produce a regression test.

Every critical component must be independently verifiable.

---

# Test Pyramid

The required testing hierarchy is

Unit Tests

↓

Integration Tests

↓

System Tests

↓

End-to-End Tests

↓

Research Validation

↓

Production Verification

Unit tests should represent the majority of tests.

---

# Directory Structure

tests/

    unit/

    integration/

    system/

    e2e/

    regression/

    datasets/

    models/

    execution/

    performance/

    fixtures/

---

# Unit Tests

Every public function requires unit tests.

Verify

Normal behavior

Edge cases

Failure conditions

Boundary values

Invalid inputs

Unit tests should not

Use network

Use exchange APIs

Depend on external services

Depend on production datasets

---

# Integration Tests

Integration tests verify interaction between modules.

Examples

Dataset Builder + Validation

Feature Engineering + Targets

Portfolio + Risk

Execution + Exchange Adapter

Metadata + Lineage

Integration tests may use temporary resources.

---

# End-to-End Tests

E2E tests verify complete workflows.

Examples

Historical Data

↓

Validation

↓

Research Dataset

↓

Feature Engineering

↓

Target Generation

↓

Model

↓

Alpha

↓

Portfolio

↓

Execution Simulation

The entire workflow must complete successfully.

---

# Regression Tests

Every bug requires

A regression test.

The bug must never reappear.

Regression tests remain permanently.

---

# Reproducibility Tests

Research must be reproducible.

Repeated execution should produce

Identical datasets

Identical features

Identical targets

Identical statistics

Identical model outputs

Identical reports

when inputs are unchanged.

---

# Data Validation Tests

Verify

Missing values

Duplicate rows

Schema correctness

Timestamp ordering

Timezone correctness

Price validity

Volume validity

Funding consistency

Order book consistency

Liquidation consistency

Dataset hashes

---

# Feature Tests

Verify

No future leakage

Expected ranges

Missing value handling

Normalization

Window correctness

Timestamp alignment

Feature version

Metadata generation

---

# Target Tests

Verify

Forward return calculations

Label correctness

Window alignment

Future timestamps

Boundary handling

Incomplete windows

Risk-adjusted targets

Overlapping horizon rules

---

# Leakage Tests

Every research dataset requires leakage tests.

Verify

Future timestamps

Target leakage

Feature leakage

Label leakage

Window leakage

Metadata leakage

No dataset proceeds if leakage exists.

---

# Statistical Tests

Verify

Information Coefficient

Rank IC

Sharpe

Sortino

Newey-West

Effective Sample Size

Trade count

Bootstrap confidence

Statistical assumptions

Statistical outputs should be deterministic.

---

