Verify

Training

Validation

Inference

Serialization

Deserialization

Prediction stability

Feature importance generation

Model metadata

Random seed control

---

# Alpha Tests

Verify

Alpha generation

Confidence calculation

Prediction uncertainty

Scaling

Normalization

Output ranges

Missing predictions

Fallback behavior

---

# Portfolio Tests

Verify

Position sizing

Risk budgeting

Volatility targeting

Exposure limits

Sector concentration

Leverage

Cash management

Allocation constraints

---

# Execution Tests

Verify

Order generation

Position transitions

Risk checks

Order rejection

Exchange formatting

Retry logic

Partial fills

Timeout handling

---

# Backtesting Tests

Verify

No future leakage

Walk-forward correctness

Transaction costs

Funding

Slippage

Capacity

Execution timing

Portfolio accounting

Performance statistics

---

# Metadata Tests

Every artifact must contain

Version

Timestamp

Hash

Configuration

Lineage

Creator

Dependencies

Metadata should be validated automatically.

---

# Configuration Tests

Verify

Schema

Required fields

Defaults

Version compatibility

Migration

Validation

Fail-fast behavior

---

# Performance Tests

Benchmark

Dataset loading

Feature engineering

Research dataset generation

Model inference

Portfolio construction

Execution simulation

Backtesting

Performance regressions should be reported.

---

# Memory Tests

Large datasets should not exceed memory budgets.

Test

Streaming

Chunking

Lazy evaluation

Garbage collection

Resource cleanup

---

# Exception Tests

Verify

Expected exceptions

Meaningful error messages

Failure recovery

Context preservation

Never silently ignore exceptions.

---

# Logging Tests

Verify important events are logged.

Do not log

Secrets

Credentials

Private keys

API tokens

---

# Security Tests

Verify

Secret handling

Access control

Configuration validation

Unsafe file access

Unauthorized operations

---

# Determinism

Repeated execution with identical inputs should produce identical outputs.

Random seeds must be controlled.

System time should never influence research results.

---

# Mocking

Mock

REST APIs

WebSockets

Exchange responses

Filesystem

Clock

Network latency

Third-party services

Avoid mocking internal business logic.

---

# Test Data

Use

Synthetic datasets

Known datasets

Deterministic fixtures

Versioned fixtures

Avoid production data in tests.

---

# Coverage

Minimum project coverage

95%

Critical modules

100%

Critical modules include

Risk

Portfolio

Execution

Validation

Governance

Configuration

Research Dataset Builder

Leakage Detection

---

# Continuous Integration

Every Pull Request must execute

Formatting

Linting

Type checking

Unit tests

Integration tests

Coverage

No merge if any stage fails.

---

# AI Rules

Whenever implementing code

Always implement corresponding tests.

Never submit untested functionality.

Never skip edge cases.

Never reduce coverage.

---

# Completion Checklist

Implementation is complete only if

✓ Unit tests pass

✓ Integration tests pass

✓ Regression tests pass

✓ Coverage target met

✓ Type checking passes

✓ Formatting passes

✓ Linting passes

✓ Performance acceptable

✓ Deterministic behavior verified

✓ Documentation updated

Otherwise implementation is incomplete.

---

# CQROS Quality Principles

Testing before deployment.

Evidence before assumptions.

Determinism before optimization.

Regression protection before new features.

Quality before speed.

Institutional reliability over rapid implementation.

These principles override development convenience.